        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a5">

                <pb facs="0711" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg611"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 accompanying Appendix
                    A.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Circular letter of Mr. Consul Scott to several
                        Hawaiian mercantile houses.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 29, 1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Your house has been importing a
                    considerable amount of foreign rice.</p>
                <p>Will it be asking you too much to state to me why foreign rice is imported into
                    this kingdom, while a large quantity of rice is raised in and exported from the
                    kingdom.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. SCOTT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
